.TH QSORT9 1.SH NAMEqsort9 \- sort lines in memory.SH SYNOPSIS\fBqsort9\fR[\-adiru] [\-f=n] [\-b=n] [file].SH DESCRIPTION\fBqsort9\fRreads a file, or the standard input, into memory, sorts its lines with aquicksort, and writes them to the standard output..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-f=\fIn\fRskip\fIn\fRblank-separated fields before the key..TP 12\fB\-r\fRreverse..TP 12\fB\-u\fRprint each line only once..TP 12\fB\-d\fRdictionary order..TP 12\fB\-i\fRignore case completely..TP 12\fB\-a\fRdo not match upper case to lower..TP 12\fB\-b=\fIn\fRa buffer of\fIn\fRbytes, or kilobytes with a\fBK\fRafter it; 4096 unless told..PPIts usage line also lists\fB\-c\fRfor a field separator other than blanks, but this build refuses\fB\-c\fRin every spelling as an unknown option; use\fBsort \-t\fRfor that..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOsort, tsort